00:21:25,861 --> 00:21:30,460
If it goes, it goes with glue.

278
00:21:30,461 --> 00:21:35,500
The trend in the automotive industry is typical of the transportation sector at large.

279
00:21:37,620 --> 00:21:42,220
Advances in the materials cars are made of have transformed the way they're held together.

280
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:49,280
The first cars were made from one material, steel, and held together with welds, bolts, and rivets.

281
00:21:50,780 --> 00:21:52,420
That's no longer the case.

282
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:56,420
Your car's composition, which used to be predominantly steel,

283
00:21:57,640 --> 00:22:03,240
has moved a lot towards things like aluminum and plastics and urethanes and synthetics as well.

284
00:22:03,241 --> 00:22:08,560
And that evolution, driven by weight reduction in many cases, as well as cost,

285
00:22:08,980 --> 00:22:14,580
has really opened up the ability for adhesives to be used in the assembly of cars.

286
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:19,600
Adhesives provide excellent bonds between dissimilar materials,

287
00:22:19,601 --> 00:22:26,400
fill and seal cracks, and don't fracture more brittle composites, as a mechanical fastener might.

288
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:31,940
One of the key adhesive applications in a car is around the windshield.

289
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:34,680
The front glass and the back glass are both urethened in,

290
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:38,000
so that's part of the structural support because, as you can tell nowadays,

291
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:39,760
the metal is nowhere near as thick as it used to be.

292
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:44,460
So a lot relies on the glass holding the roof up in a rollover.

293
00:22:44,461 --> 00:22:51,460
During a windshield replacement, you can see how strong that urethane bond is when you try to remove it.

294
00:22:51,461 --> 00:22:56,460
This will cut that glue that's in here, which is usually about a half inch, maybe three quarters of an inch wide.

295
00:22:59,460 --> 00:23:03,460
Once the broken windshield's out, it's time to apply the glue.

296
00:23:03,461 --> 00:23:07,460
175 degree urethane, which cools and cures quickly.

297
00:23:07,461 --> 00:23:09,660
We've got about eight minutes to get the windshield in.

298
00:23:09,661 --> 00:23:11,460
We want to get in there as quickly as we can.

299
00:23:14,460 --> 00:23:19,460
So it'll be about an hour before they can drive away safely.

300
00:23:23,780 --> 00:23:27,740
When the adhesive is thought about in the front end of this design,

301
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:32,720
it's providing lighter weight, less parts, ultimately less cost.

302
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:36,560
There's a lot of labor involved with drilling a hole,

303
00:23:36,940 --> 00:23:40,480
placing the rivet, and making that component adhere to one another.

304
00:23:40,481 --> 00:23:45,700
A key breakthrough to replacing mechanical fasteners occurred in 1953.

305
00:23:46,780 --> 00:23:49,360
Chemist Dr. Vernon Kreebel of Hartford, Connecticut,

306
00:23:49,760 --> 00:23:54,480
solved the instability problem of a new adhesive that his chemist's son, Robert, had brought him.

307
00:23:55,320 --> 00:23:58,120
Vernon Kreebel developed a cure inhibition system

308
00:23:58,121 --> 00:24:03,400
for a unique liquid bonding resin that hardened anaerobically or in the absence of air.

309
00:24:03,860 --> 00:24:07,540
As long as it's in contact with air, it remains a liquid.

310
00:24:07,541 --> 00:24:11,980
You put it onto a nut and bolt or onto a bearing or any shaft-mounted part,

311
00:24:12,340 --> 00:24:15,500
and what it does is it wicks its way between the threads.

312
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:21,300
As soon as it's in the contact of metal and there's no oxygen for it to remain stable,

313
00:24:21,380 --> 00:24:23,040
it hardens to essentially a tough plastic.

314
00:24:25,940 --> 00:24:31,900
The product, Loctite, solved the problem of loose nuts and bolts in machines and appliances

315
00:24:31,901 --> 00:24:35,760
and is still the cornerstone of the company's adhesives business.

316
00:24:37,540 --> 00:24:44,540
Loctite products can be found in many of the cars on the road.

317
00:24:46,340 --> 00:24:50,540
But the adhesive's usefulness is most dramatic in high-performance vehicles,

318
00:24:50,541 --> 00:24:54,540
where vibration is intense and you can't afford to have a screw loose.

319
00:24:54,541 --> 00:25:00,540
The Daytona 500, virtually every one of those cars is held together.

320
00:25:00,541 --> 00:25:04,540
The threaded parts especially are held together with Loctite thread lockers.

321
00:25:04,541 --> 00:25:14,908
In the 60s, part of racing was cleaning the track up, and they would literally go around the track with a sweeper and clean up nuts and bolts that may have come off

